+## TEXTURE so the highlight is a soft field rather than one uniform sweep — which
+## is the entire difference from the flat `roughness = 0.85` this replaces.
+##
+## The grain is coarsened from the kit's 4.0 tiles/m to 3.0, a 14 mm mottle: see
+## the header. `dirty` 0..1 is only ever 1 for the decal body, the one that lies on
+## the floor. Note the darkening budget — the rams_body wear term and the weather
+## grime are the ONLY two, there is no AO map and no baked vertex wear, so the
+## cream stays cream (0.90 -> 0.78 at the darkest blotch) instead of agreeing on
+## black the way three subtle darkenings always do.
+func _paper(dirty: float) -> StandardMaterial3D:
+	var d: float = clampf(dirty, 0.0, 1.0)
+	var m: StandardMaterial3D = PK.rams_body(PAPER, 0.16 + d * 0.14)
+	PK.scale_detail(m, 0.75)
+	# Board fibres scatter at grazing angles. This is also the cheapest way to give
+	# a pale card an edge against a pale wall without an outline shader.
+	PK.edge_light(m, 0.20, 0.55)
